# Day 33 - Spiral Matrix

## Problem Statement
Given an `m × n` matrix, return all elements of the matrix in **spiral order**.

## Code

class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> spiralOrder(vector<vector<int>>& matrix) {
        int m = matrix.size();
        int n = matrix[0].size();

        int srow = 0, erow = m - 1;
        int scol = 0, ecol = n - 1;

        vector<int> ans;

        while (srow <= erow && scol <= ecol) {

            // Top row
            for (int i = scol; i <= ecol; i++) {
                ans.push_back(matrix[srow][i]);
            }

            // Right column
            for (int j = srow + 1; j <= erow; j++) {
                ans.push_back(matrix[j][ecol]);
            }

            // Bottom row
            if (srow < erow) {
                for (int i = ecol - 1; i >= scol; i--) {
                    ans.push_back(matrix[erow][i]);
                }
            }

            // Left column
            if (scol < ecol) {
                for (int j = erow - 1; j > srow; j--) {
                    ans.push_back(matrix[j][scol]);
                }
            }

            // Shrink boundaries
            srow++;
            erow--;
            scol++;
            ecol--;
        }

        return ans;
    }
};



## Time Complexity
**O(m × n)**

## Space Complexity
**O(1)** (excluding the output array)

> The returned vector `ans` stores the required output and is not counted as auxiliary space.

## Approach
This solution uses the **Boundary Traversal** technique. Four boundaries (`srow`, `erow`, `scol`, and `ecol`) define the current layer of the matrix. In each iteration, the algorithm traverses the **top row**, **right column**, **bottom row**, and **left column** in sequence, adding each element to the answer. Before traversing the bottom row and left column, boundary checks are performed to avoid visiting the same row or column twice in matrices with a single row or column. After completing one layer, all four boundaries are shrunk inward, and the process repeats until every element has been visited.

